<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7789"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 3:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you very much for the link, Ok I was going through the Crime Library&#39;s e-book and thought of something. They gave us three of the letters and the two poems from 1974-1978 to work with. So we know he wrote them before he wrote the outline for his story, so things like the factor X and the black out are more than likey in here. It would be interesting to see if we could get ahold of the rest of those letters from 1974-1978. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
