</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 12:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok lets say for example that the Otero murders do not have the same motive as the others. IE reason for the break into chapters, Let&#39;s say that BTK was a student of Joes In the Panama death squad, and decided to come to Kansas to pay him a visit, Joe didn&#39;t want to see him because he is a nut. So he killed them, didn&#39;t want Joe telling anyone who he was. or he just wanted to kill them, That would be why he can&#39;t be caught, that is why all the theories we have are not paning out. If we erase any theroy that we have about his past before the murders, then we can start with A Serial Killer is Born, In this case, he was already killing, but in those days in Panama, he was under orders from the government, so when he came to Kansas, he would have been on the out takes as he says of the law. If we concentrate on the actual cases, we can skip the theories and say, Yes, His MO ID Ruse chapter is how he got into the victims homes, it was all part of his previous training, The reason we have those puzzles, all part of his training and thinking, he thinks of everything in number letter sequences, including street names. they don&#39;t mean street names to him.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
